        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(android): add cron job management controls",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nAndroid currently surfaces gateway cron jobs as status/detail information, but cron operators still need to switch back to another client to run, pause, edit, or remove scheduled work. This PR makes the Android settings cron surface actionable so mobile users can manage gateway cron jobs from the same place they inspect them.\n\n## Summary\n\n- Adds Android Settings cron-job management controls to inspect, run now, enable/disable, edit, and delete gateway cron jobs.\n- Extends cron detail parsing to retain editable schedule, payload, session target, wake mode, and run-history metadata.\n- Adds a dedicated Android cron screenshot/proof workflow and screenshot scene for the new management surface.\n\n## Implementation notes\n\n- Keeps the existing cron list/detail request guard and extends it with run history plus action state.\n- Sends mutations through gateway RPCs: `cron.run`, `cron.update`, `cron.remove`, and `cron.runs`.\n- Updates Android native i18n source entries and Android docs for the new screenshot scene.\n\n## Evidence\n\nLocal lightweight checks only:\n\n- `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD` ✅\n- `bash -n scripts/android-screenshots.sh` ✅\n- `tsx scripts/native-app-i18n.ts check` ✅\n\nGitHub Actions proof:\n\n- Android Cron Management Proof: https://github.com/snowzlmbot/openclaw/actions/runs/28898897301 ✅ passed (build + unit test APK, emulator screenshot scene, APK and screenshot artifacts uploaded)\n\n## Risk and rollback\n\n- Risk is limited to the Android settings cron-management surface and the added proof workflow.\n- Rollback is straightforward: revert this PR to restore the prior read-only cron detail UI.",
